		"notes": "\n\t<p><i>Simulacrums created to bear the cosmic burden of their progenitor's sins. Exist as a nigh-exact scapegoat. Psychopomps considered shabti profane.</i></p>\n\t<p></p>\n\t<p><strong>AC</strong> 10, <strong>HP</strong> 5, <strong>ATK</strong> 1 shortsword +0 (1d6) or 1 spell +2, <strong>MV</strong> near, <strong>S</strong> +0, <strong>D</strong> +0, <strong>C</strong> +1, <strong>I</strong> +0, <strong>W</strong> -1, <strong>Ch</strong> +2, <strong>AL</strong> L, <strong>LV</strong> 1</p><p></p>\n\t<p><strong>Aging Touch (CHA Spell)</strong>. DC 12. One target in close takes 1d4 STR damage, paralyzed at 0 STR.</p><p></p><p><strong>Flicker (CHA Spell)</strong>. DC 12. Self. Phase in and out for 1d4 rounds. Attacks against shabti have DISADV.</p><p></p><p><strong>Immortal</strong>. Shabti do not age naturally and can't die of old age. Cannot become undead.</p><p></p>\n\t<p><i>Shadowfinder Complete Bestiary</i></p>",
